; FILL flood-fills the region containing the turtle, bounded by
; whatever lines are already drawn, with the turtle's current pen color.

REPEAT 4 [FD 100 RT 90]
PENUP
SETXY 300 200
PENDOWN
SETPENCOLOR 255 200 0
FILL

; CLEAR erases fills along with lines/labels -- draw and fill a second,
; larger square to confirm.
CLEAR
REPEAT 4 [FD 150 RT 90]
PENUP
SETXY 325 175
PENDOWN
SETPENCOLOR 0 150 255
FILL

; A FILL freezes its boundary at the moment it's called -- a line drawn
; through the filled region afterward does NOT retroactively carve it
; into two separately-colored halves the next time the canvas redraws.
; This vertical line spans the square's full height, splitting it into
; a left and right half; both halves should stay fully filled, not just
; the half containing the FILL's own (325, 175) seed point.
PENUP
SETXY 350 100
PENDOWN
SETXY 350 250
